The defect is twofold: the base case returns `1` for both `F(0)` and `F(1)`, and the linear recursion cannot meet the `n=100000`/one-second constraint. I’m replacing it with the standard fast-doubling recurrence, keeping the public API and changing only `buggy.py`.
